    "m_FunctionBody": "// The room appears behind a front that sweeps out from _RevealOrigin (the door the room was entered through). Floors\n// come first: height above the origin counts as extra distance (_HeightDelay), so walls rise behind the front. Value\n// noise breaks the front up, and the band just behind it glows (_EdgeColor, HDR, so bloom picks it up).\n// String-mode functions can't declare helpers, so the noise is inline: smooth value noise over a hashed lattice.\nfloat3 p = WorldPosition * _NoiseScale;\nfloat3 cellIndex = floor(p);\nfloat3 t = frac(p);\nt = t * t * (3.0 - 2.0 * t);\nfloat noise = 0.0;\n[unroll] for (int corner = 0; corner < 8; corner++)\n{\n    float3 o = float3(corner & 1, (corner >> 1) & 1, (corner >> 2) & 1);\n    float h = frac(sin(dot(cellIndex + o, float3(127.1, 311.7, 74.7))) * 43758.5453);\n    float3 w = lerp(1.0 - t, t, o);\n    noise += h * w.x * w.y * w.z;\n}\n\nfloat height = max(WorldPosition.y - _RevealOrigin.y, 0.0);\nfloat distanceToOrigin = length(WorldPosition.xz - _RevealOrigin.xz) + height * _HeightDelay + noise * _NoiseAmount;\nfloat front = _Reveal * (_RevealRadius + _EdgeWidth + _NoiseAmount);\n\nAlpha = distanceToOrigin <= front ? 1.0 : 0.0;\nfloat edge = 1.0 - saturate((front - distanceToOrigin) / max(_EdgeWidth, 0.0001));\nfloat settled = saturate((1.0 - _Reveal) * 8.0);\nfloat isFloor = WorldNormal.y > 0.5 ? 1.0 : 0.0;\nBaseColor = lerp(_WallColor.rgb, _FloorColor.rgb, isFloor);\nEmission = _EdgeColor.rgb * edge * edge * Alpha * settled;"
}

